      description: "Fibrosis is an abnormal wound-repair program in which fibroblasts proliferate, become myofibroblasts, and deposit collagen-rich extracellular matrix that stiffens the lung. Nintedanib inhibits several receptor tyrosine kinases that transmit fibroblast and vascular growth signals. Pirfenidone has antifibrotic and anti-inflammatory effects, but its precise human molecular target is not established; experimental effects include reduced TGF-beta-driven collagen programs. Both slow average decline rather than reverse scar, so stable lung function can represent treatment benefit even when the patient does not feel dramatically better.",
