      usedToTreat: "Rapid treatment or prevention of bronchospasm in reversible obstructive airway disease and prevention of exercise-induced bronchospasm. It relieves tightened airway smooth muscle within minutes but does not treat the airway inflammation that drives asthma attacks, so frequent need signals inadequate control rather than a reason to rely on albuterol alone.",
      description: "Albuterol is the racemic, rapid-onset short-acting beta2 agonist used as a rescue bronchodilator. It contains active R-albuterol and much less active S-albuterol. By raising cyclic AMP in airway smooth muscle, it relaxes constricted bronchi and improves airflow within minutes. The opening distinction is essential: albuterol treats bronchospasm, not the mucosal edema, eosinophilic inflammation, and mucus biology that make asthma dangerous. If doses are needed more often, give less relief, or wear off early, the disease may be worsening even when each puff briefly helps. Repeated high doses can shift potassium into cells and increase lactate, tremor, and tachycardia.",
