      usedToTreat: "Product-specific maintenance bronchodilation in COPD and, only when combined with an inhaled corticosteroid in an appropriate product and prescribed regimen, asthma maintenance or anti-inflammatory reliever/MART treatment. Standalone formoterol does not treat acute deterioration and must not be used alone in asthma.",
      description: "Formoterol is unusual among LABAs because it begins bronchodilation rapidly like a rescue beta agonist yet remains active for about 12 hours. Its molecular balance of water solubility and lipophilicity lets some drug reach beta2 receptors quickly while another fraction remains in airway membranes as a depot. This property allows low-dose ICS-formoterol combinations to serve as anti-inflammatory relievers or MART under validated plans. It does not make standalone nebulized formoterol an asthma rescue drug: products such as Perforomist are COPD maintenance treatments, and any LABA used in asthma must be paired with an inhaled corticosteroid.",
      mechanism: "Formoterol binds beta2 receptors with high intrinsic efficacy. Gs activates adenylyl cyclase, cyclic AMP rises, and protein kinase A reduces myosin light-chain kinase activity and calcium-dependent contraction, rapidly relaxing airway smooth muscle. The molecule's polar groups allow relatively fast access through airway fluid, while lipophilic portions partition into the cell membrane and slowly return to the receptor, extending action. Systemic receptor stimulation shifts potassium into skeletal muscle and increases tremor, heart rate, glucose, and lactate. Formoterol does not directly switch off inflammatory transcription; the inhaled corticosteroid in an AIR/MART inhaler supplies that protection with each symptom-driven dose.",
