      contraindications: ["Primary treatment of status asthmaticus or an acute episode requiring intensive measures", "Hypersensitivity to ingredients; do not combine with another LABA-containing medicine"],
      nursingEssentials: ["Document whether the plan is scheduled maintenance, AIR only, or MART and teach the exact strength, puffs, daily ceiling, and when to seek urgent care.", "Assess technique and adherence, rinse and spit after maintenance doses, monitor oral cavity, exacerbations, rescue use, and COPD pneumonia cues."],
      interactions: ["Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors can increase systemic budesonide exposure; other sympathomimetics and LABAs add formoterol toxicity.", "Nonselective beta blockers oppose bronchodilation; diuretics can magnify hypokalemia; abrupt systemic-steroid withdrawal can expose adrenal insufficiency."],
      keyLabs: ["Symptoms, exacerbations, reliever frequency, peak flow/spirometry, oral exam, inhaler technique, and adherence", "Potassium, glucose, adrenal function, growth, bone or eye assessment when cumulative exposure makes them relevant"],
      nclexTraps: ["ICS-formoterol can be AIR/MART because formoterol is rapid-onset; this logic does not apply to salmeterol combinations.", "Guideline-supported reliever use still requires the correct product and prescribed maximum; it is not permission for unlimited puffs."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Asthma strengths and ages differ; growth and technique require monitoring. AIR/MART recommendations are age- and product-specific.", "Older adults have more pneumonia, bone, eye, cardiac, glucose, and polypharmacy risk.", "Budesonide has substantial pregnancy experience; maintain asthma control with the lowest effective prescribed regimen and individualized lactation review."),
      sourceNote: "Current U.S. SYMBICORT labeling plus GINA 2026 strategy: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=fafa4cf1-99c2-43d5-73ad-51f256de3be0 ; https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf",
