      mechanism: "Fluticasone binds intracellular glucocorticoid receptors with high affinity, moves to the nucleus, induces anti-inflammatory genes, and represses NF-kappaB and AP-1 pathways, reducing inflammatory-cell survival and mediator release. Salmeterol activates beta2-Gs-adenylyl cyclase-cAMP-PKA signaling to reduce myosin light-chain kinase and calcium-dependent smooth-muscle contraction. Its lipophilic side chain anchors near a receptor exosite and prolongs action, but receptor access is too slow for rescue use. Corticosteroid signaling can increase beta2-receptor expression and LABA signaling can support glucocorticoid-receptor function, explaining maintenance synergy. Neither component immediately substitutes for emergency treatment of severe airflow obstruction.",
